  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Leave the EU, end EU free movement, five‑year moratorium on unskilled immigration, five years’ tax/NI before benefits; cut overseas aid to 0.2% of GNI; NHS +£12bn, £1.5bn for mental health/dementia, restore social care funding, increase Carer’s Allowance, scrap bedroom tax, pay Housing Benefit to under‑25s; 6,000 extra posts across police/prisons/borders; leave ECHR, repeal HRA; promote British culture and add national bank holidays; repeal Climate Change Act and end most renewables subsidies. TEXT_E: NHS funding up by at least £8bn by 2020, 7‑day NHS, integrate health and social care, focus on mental health; 30 hours’ free childcare; protect nature (Blue Belt), plant 11m trees, expand flood defences; maintain 0.7% GNI on international development; ‘rewarding work’ with Tax‑Free Minimum Wage link, benefit cap reduction and freeze, ‘earn or learn’; four‑year residency before in‑work benefits; target net migration in the tens of thousands; EU in/out referendum; stronger policing, counter‑extremism powers, British Bill of Rights.",
  "reasoning": "Given high weight on Care with notable but secondary Loyalty and mid‑level Proportionality/Authority, TEXT_E balances in‑group care (NHS, childcare) with broader harm‑reduction (environment, maintaining 0.7% aid) while stressing proportionality ('rewarding work', residency before benefits) and moderate authority/loyalty (immigration targets, security, EU referendum). TEXT_D provides substantial domestic care but strongly prioritizes Loyalty/Authority (sovereignty, hard borders, citizenship revocation) and reduces broader care (aid cuts, climate rollback), making it a less precise fit to a care‑led, proportionate, moderately loyal profile.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
